{
  "requirement": "During one call to `Validator::verify`, direct reads by the criterion and\nreads served by the SDK's agent tools record inputs in the same\n`ValidationContext`. For example, if criterion code reads a test and the agent\nthen reads its helper, both node fingerprints accompany the returned answer.\nA subsequent verification starts with an empty dependency list.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural obligations are met.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n- Direct criterion reads and agent-tool reads must record into the same `ValidationContext` during one `Validator::verify` call.\n- Each `verify` call must start with an empty dependency list.\n\n**Single shared context per call**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/runtime.rs#impl[Validator<D>]#1/fn[verify]` builds a fresh `ValidationContext::configured(...)` for each call. It passes `&mut ctx` to `criterion.execute` and returns `ctx.dependencies()` in the `Fingerprinted` answer. That is the single context for a call.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#1/fn[configured]` initializes `observations: Default::default()`, so a later verification starts with an empty list.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#struct[ValidationContext]` holds one `observations` mutex-guarded `Vec<Dependency<...>>`.\n\n**Direct reads**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#2/fn[read_snapshot]` calls `prepare_read` and then `record_read` on `self`.\n- `record_read` and `observe_edges_by` push into the same `observations` vector.\n\n**Agent-tool reads**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]` passes `self.ctx`, the same context, to `agent.run(request, self.ctx)`. It also records the prepared input nodes through `prepare_read` and `observe_edges_by`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` takes that `&ValidationContext` and stores it in `GraphSession.inspection`. It queues the request inputs as pending `Dependency::Node` values.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[dispatch]` serves `read_node` and `outgoing_edges` through `inspection.prepare_read` and `inspection.prepare_edges`. It queues pending dependencies, and fallback tool dependencies are queued the same way.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[delivered]` drains `pending` into `inspection.record_read` and `inspection.observe_edges`. Those are the same recorders the direct reads use.\n\nSo the criterion's direct reads and the agent's tool reads both accumulate in one `ValidationContext`. That matches the example of a test read followed by its helper, where both fingerprints accompany the answer. I assessed only the structural obligations, and no gap was found.",
  "references": "2c35862fa48dbc05e8825f322f614b0f35937ab779b0239d61752080a67691e4",
